{"step_index":218,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:43:20Z","thinking":"**Formalizing domination numbers in Lean**\n\nAttempting to formalize the known relationship: (nontrivial) implies total domination number is less than or equal to the roman domination number. The proof is confirmed to be exact, beautiful, complete, and constructive. Proceeding by meticulously verifying the definitions of total domination number and roman domination number within the `GraphInvariantsComputable.lean` reference file. This step is crucial for establishing a solid foundation.\n\n\n**Analyzing domination number definitions**\n\nVerifying that if a set `S` satisfies the `IsTotalDominatingSet` property, then the `totalDominationNumber` is indeed less than or equal to the cardinality of `S`. The `totalDominationNumber` is defined as the minimum cardinality of any total dominating set, and if `S` is such a set, then the minimum must be less than or equal to the cardinality of `S`. This aligns with the overall goal. Further investigation of the `romanDominationNumber` definition is needed.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"import Mathlib\\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\\n\\nopen SimpleGraph\\n\\nvariable {V : Type*} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\nvariable (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\\n\\nlemma minCard_le {p : Finset V → Prop} [DecidablePred p] {s : Finset V} (hs : p s) :\\n    GraphCalc.minCard p ≤ s.card := by\\n  sorry\\n\"","Description":"\"Testing minCard_le in scratch_test.lean\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_40a99333/scratch_test.lean\"","toolAction":"\"Writing minCard_le in scratch_test.lean\"","toolSummary":"\"Write minCard_le scratch\""}}]}
