{"step_index":266,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:44:59Z","thinking":"**Verifying graph domination property**\n\nThe `h_has_td` assumption implies that for any vertex *v* within the graph, there must be an adjacent vertex *u*. This is due to the definition of total domination number. The provided `lemma exists_adj_of_hasTotalDominationNumber` is likely to formally represent this property of total domination.\n```lean\nlemma exists_adj_of_hasTotalDominationNumber {V : Type*} [Fint\n```\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"import Mathlib\\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\\n\\nopen SimpleGraph\\n\\nlemma exists_adj_of_hasTotalDominationNumber {V : Type*} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (h : GraphCalc.HasTotalDominationNumber G) (v : V) :\\n    ∃ u : V, G.Adj v u := by\\n  unfold GraphCalc.HasTotalDominationNumber GraphCalc.HasWitness at h\\n  obtain ⟨s, _, hs⟩ := h\\n  unfold GraphCalc.IsTotalDominatingSet at hs\\n  obtain ⟨u, _, hu⟩ := hs v\\n  exact ⟨u, hu⟩\\n\"","Description":"\"Testing exists_adj_of_hasTotalDominationNumber\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_40a99333/scratch_test.lean\"","toolAction":"\"Writing exists_adj lemma in scratch_test.lean\"","toolSummary":"\"Write exists_adj lemma\""}}]}
